{"name":"Korma","hex":"#804e2c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"korma","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A curry made from various spices especially coriander and cumin; and often with yoghurt sauce or nuts.\n\n A curry of meat slowly braised with ghee.\n\n A mild curry (typically the mildest on a given menu), often with a fragrant coconut sauce.","A curry of meat slowly braised with ghee."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/korma"}],"entries":[{"title":"Korma","blocks":[{"text":"Korma, kurma, qorma or qurma is a curry dish originating in the Indian subcontinent influenced by Mughlai cuisine, versions of which later were modified to Anglo-Indian and then to British tastes. It consists of meat or vegetables braised with yogurt, water or stock, and spices to produce a thick sauce or gravy. The flavours of kormas are less intense than those of meat-containing dishes, and the fragrances more aromatic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Chicken_Korma.JPG/330px-Chicken_Korma.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Korma","wikidata":"Q1979684"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Chicken_White_Qorma_%28Korma%29.JPG/250px-Chicken_White_Qorma_%28Korma%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Chicken_White_Qorma_%28Korma%29.JPG/500px-Chicken_White_Qorma_%28Korma%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Chicken_White_Qorma_%28Korma%29.JPG/250px-Chicken_White_Qorma_%28Korma%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChicken_White_Qorma_(Korma).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/c